      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T18:31:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This topic of a future 128-bit `int` type has come up several times in code reviews. We should make a decision and document it in a file.\n\nThere are three options:\n- My preference: Accept the prevalent assumption that `int` is 32 bits and cast `int` to `int64_t`.\n- Cast `int` to `long long`.\n- Use `int32_t` instead of `int`. Then it\u0027s safe to cast `int32_t` to `int64_t`.",
      "parentUuid": "af9cd395_b2b352c6",
      "revId": "11a02da8babeccc2a2731b27b6f00ee3cc029c11",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
